course: dictionary
lesson: 3750
title: Fluid: a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fluid can be a noun or an adjective, so its job changes with the sentence. As a noun, a fluid is a substance that can flow, like water, juice or air. «Whether you have a cold or a fever, the body needs fluids and energy.» Here fluids means drinks such as water.
explain: Use the words around it as clues. In «Deep in each ear are three curved tubes full of fluid», fluid names a thing, the liquid inside the tubes, so it is a noun. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it describing something? A thing is a noun.
explain: As an adjective, fluid describes movement that is smooth and easy, or something that can change. Try your meaning in the sentence: «fluid movements» means smooth movements, and that makes sense. Swap your meaning in to check it.
fact: A fluid is a substance that can flow, such as a liquid or a gas.
fact: Air and water are both fluids.
fact: «Fluids» often means drinks, like water and juice, as in «drink plenty of fluids».
fact: As an adjective, «fluid» means moving smoothly and easily, or able to change.
fact: In «fluid fills the gap», fluid is a liquid that moves into a space, which is how a blister forms.
exercise: «When you are ill, your body needs rest, fluids and time.» In this sentence, what are fluids? | Tiny germs | Hard bones | Blankets and pillows | *Drinks such as water and juice
exercise: Dad says, «Air and water are both fluids.» What is a fluid? | *A substance that can flow, like a liquid or a gas | A solid thing that always keeps its shape | A kind of loud sound | A bright light you can see in the dark
exercise: «Her fluid movements made the dancers look effortless.» What does fluid mean here? | Stuck and slow | Very loud | Wet and sticky | *Smooth and easy
test: «Rubbing makes skin layers slide apart and fluid fills the gap, which is a blister.» What is the fluid in this sentence? | A hard crust | Dry air | A bone | *A liquid that fills a gap in the skin
test: In «The cat made fluid, graceful jumps across the wall», what does fluid tell us? | *The jumps moved smoothly and easily | The jumps were very loud | The cat was asleep | The cat is made of liquid
exam: In «drink plenty of fluids», what does fluids mean? | Smooth movements | Hard, dry things | A type of germ | *Drinks such as water and juice
